[[es:Mito japonés de la creación de los dioses]]
[[ja:神産み]]

[[File:Izanagi Izanami genealogía.PNG|thumb|300px|Genealogy of Izanagi and Izanami according to the [[Kojiki]]]]
In [[Japanese mythology]], the story of the {{nihongo|birth of the gods|神産み|'''Kamiumi'''}} occurs after the creation of Japan (''[[Kuniumi]]'') and refers to the birth of the ''[[kami]]'', descendants of [[Izanagi]] and [[Izanami]].

==Story==
According to the [[Kojiki]], various gods were born from the relationship between Izanagi and Izanami until the fire deity, Kagutsuchi, at birth burned Izanami's genitals and wounded her fatally. Izanagi, witnessing the death of his beloved wife, in rage takes the ten-grasp<ref group="nb" name="grasp">A "grasp" is the breadth of four fingers when the hand is clenched.</ref> sabre and crushes his child, Kagusuchi. A number of gods were born from the blood and remains of Kagutsuchi. Subsequently, Izanagi went to the land of [[Yomi]] (the world of the dead) to find Izanami, however when he found her, she had become a rotting corpse and from her parts other gods had arisen, causing the flight of Izanagi to the world of the living. Then Izanagi performs the [[misogi]] [[ritual purification]] through which more gods are born.  The last of these are the three most important gods of [[Shinto]]: [[Amaterasu]], goddess of the sun; [[Tsukuyomi]], deity of the moon; and [[Susanoo]], god of the sea.

===Birth of the gods===
[[File:Izanami genealogía.PNG|thumb|300px|Gods born during the agony and death of Izanami.]]
After having created the Eight Large Islands (''[[Ōyashima]]'') and other islands during the [[Kuniumi|creation of Japan]], Izanagi and Izanami decided to give birth to other gods, among them the {{nihongo|''Katakurokushin''|家宅六神}}, deities of the wind, trees and meadows, all born spontaneously:

# {{nihongo|'''[[Ohokotooshio]]'''|大事忍男神}}
# {{nihongo|'''[[Ihatsuchibiko]]'''|石土毘古神}}
# {{nihongo|'''[[Ihasuhime]]'''|石巣比売神}}
# {{nihongo|'''[[Ohotohiwake]]'''|大戸日別神}}
# {{nihongo|'''[[Ame-no-fukio]]'''|天之吹男神}}
# {{nihongo|'''[[Ohoyabiko]]'''|大屋毘古神}}
# {{nihongo|'''[[Kazamotsuwake-no-oshio]]'''|風木津別之忍男神}}
# {{nihongo|'''[[Ohowatatsumi]]'''|大綿津見神}}
# {{nihongo|'''[[Hayaakitsuhiko]]'''|速秋津日子神}}
# {{nihongo|'''[[Hayaakitsuhime]]'''|速秋津比売神}}
#: From the relationship between Hayaakitsuhiko and Hayaakitsuhime the following gods were born:
## {{nihongo|'''[[Ahanagi]]'''|沫那藝神}}
## {{nihongo|'''[[Ahanami]]'''|沫那美神}}
## {{nihongo|'''[[Tsuranagi]]'''|頬那藝神}}
## {{nihongo|'''[[Tsuranami]]'''|頬那美神}}
## {{nihongo|'''[[Ame-no-mikumari]]'''|天之水分神}}
## {{nihongo|'''[[Kuni-no-mikumari]]'''|国之水分神}}
## {{nihongo|'''[[Ame-no-kuhizamochi]]'''|天之久比奢母智神}}
## {{nihongo|'''[[Kuni-no-kuhizamochi]]'''|国之久比奢母智神}}
# {{nihongo|'''[[Shina-Tsu-Hiko|Shinatsuhiko]]'''|志那都比古神}}
# {{nihongo|'''[[Kukunochi]]'''|久久能智神}}
# {{nihongo|'''[[Ohoyamatsumi]]'''|大山津見神}}
# {{nihongo|'''[[Kaya-no-hime]]'''|鹿屋野比売神}}, also known as {{nihongo|'''Nozuchi'''|野椎神}}
#: From the relationship between Ohoyamatsumi and Kaya-no-hime the following gods were born:
## {{nihongo|'''[[Ame-no-sazuchi]]'''|天之狭土神}}
## {{nihongo|'''[[Kuni-no-sazuchi]]'''|国之狭土神}}
## {{nihongo|'''[[Ame-no-sagiri]]'''|天之狭霧神}}
## {{nihongo|'''[[Kuni-no-sagiri]]'''|国之狭霧神}}
## {{nihongo|'''[[Ame-no-kurado]]'''|天之闇戸神}}
## {{nihongo|'''[[Kuni-no-kurado]]'''|国之闇戸神}}
## {{nihongo|'''[[Ohotomatohiko]]'''|大戸惑子神}}
## {{nihongo|'''[[Ohotomatohime]]'''|大戸惑女神}}
# {{nihongo|'''[[Tori-no-ihakusubune]]'''|鳥之石楠船神}}, also known as {{nihongo|'''Ame-no-torifune'''|天鳥船}}
# {{nihongo|'''[[Ohogetsuhime]]'''|大宜都比売神}}
# {{nihongo|'''[[Kagutsuchi|Hi-no-yagihayao]]'''|火之夜藝速男神}}, also known as {{nihongo|'''Hi-no-kagabiko'''|火之炫毘古神}} and {{nihongo|'''Hi-no-kagutsuchi'''|火之迦具土神}}
#: During Kagustuchi's birth, Izanami's genitals were burned and she was mortally wounded. In her agony, from her vomit, urine and feces more gods were born.
# {{nihongo|'''[[Kanayamabiko]]'''|金山毘古神}}, born from the [[vomit]] and [[feces]] of Izanami
# {{nihongo|'''[[Kanayamabime]]'''|金山毘売神}}, born from the vomit and feces of Izanami
# {{nihongo|'''[[Haniyasubiko]]'''|波邇夜須毘古神}}, born from the feces of Izanami
# {{nihongo|'''[[Haniyasubime]]'''|波邇夜須毘売神}}, born from the feces of Izanami
# {{nihongo|'''[[Mitsuhanome]]'''|彌都波能売神}}, born from the [[urine]] of Izanami
# {{nihongo|'''[[Wakumusuhi]]'''|和久産巣日神}}, born from the urine of Izanami
#: Wakumusuhi had a daughter:
## {{nihongo|'''[[Toyouke-Ōmikami|Toyouke]]'''|豊宇気毘売神}}

===Death of Kagutsuchi===
After the agony, Izanami dies. At the time Izanagi crept moaning about the body and mourned her death. From his tears {{nihongo|Nakisawame|泣 沢 女神}} was born. Subsequently Izanagi buries Izanami on [[Mount Hiba]]. His sadness turned into anger and he decides to kill Kagutsuchi with a ten-grasp<ref group="nb" name="grasp"/> sword called {{nihongo|[[Ame-no-ohabari]]|天之尾羽張|extra=also known as Itsu-no-ohabari}}.

From the blood of Kagutsuchi the following gods emerged:

# {{nihongo|'''[[Ihasaku]]'''|石折神}}
# {{nihongo|'''[[Nesaku]]'''|根折神}}
# {{nihongo|'''[[Ihatsutsunoo]]'''|石筒之男神}}
#: The gods above were born from the blood that fell from the tip of the sword in the rocks.
# {{nihongo|'''[[Mikahayahi]]'''|甕速日神}}
# {{nihongo|'''[[Hihayahi]]'''|樋速日神}}
# {{nihongo|'''[[Takemikagutsuchinoo]]'''|建御雷之男神}}, also known as {{nihongo|'''Takefutsu'''|建布都神}} or {{nihongo|'''Toyofutsu'''|豊布都神}}
#: The gods above were born from the blood that fell from the blade of the sword.
# {{nihongo|'''[[Kuraokami]]'''|闇淤加美神}}
# {{nihongo|'''[[Kuramitsuha]]'''|闇御津羽神}}
#: The gods above were born from the blood that fell from the handle of the sword.

Also, from the body of Kagutsuchi the following gods were born:
# {{nihongo|'''[[Masakayamatsumi]]'''|正鹿山津見神}}, emerged from Kagutsuchi's head;
# {{nihongo|'''[[Odoyamatsumi]]'''|淤縢山津見神}}, from the chest;
# {{nihongo|'''[[Okuyamatsumi]]'''|奥山津見神}}, from the abdomen;
# {{nihongo|'''[[Kurayamatsumi]]'''|闇山津見神}}, from the genitals;
# {{nihongo|'''[[Shigiyamatsumi]]'''|志藝山津見神}}, from the left arm;
# {{nihongo|'''[[Hayamatsumi]]'''|羽山津見神}}, from the right arm;
# {{nihongo|'''[[Harayamatsumi]]'''|原山津見神}}, from the left foot;
# {{nihongo|'''[[Toyamatsumi]]'''|戸山津見神}}, from the right foot.

===Land of Yomi===
Izanagi then decides to bring back Izanami and goes to [[Yomi]], the underworld. Crossing the gates to that world, he meets Izanami and says to her:

{{quote|The countries that you and me have created have not been completed yet. Let us return!|<ref group="nb">「あなたと一緒に創った国土はまだ完成していません。帰りましょう。」. ''[[Kojiki]]''</ref>}}

Izanami replies:

{{quote|¡Too bad you did not come before, for I have eaten in the country of Yomi! ... however, I will consult with the gods of Yomi. Under no circumstances you may look at me!|<ref group="nb">「黄泉の国の食べ物を食べてしまったので、生き返ることはできません」「黄泉神と相談しましょう。お願いですから、私の姿は見ないで下さいね。」. ''[[Kojiki]]''</ref>}}

On saying this, Izanami entered the palace of these gods. However, time passed and she did not return and Izanagi began to despair. So he broke one of the tines of his ornamental comb mizura that he wore in the left bun of his hair, lit it in order to light the place and decided to enter the world of dead. He manages to find Izanami but is surprised to see that she lost her beauty and had become a rotting corpse, covered with maggots. Of her body were born the eight Gods of thunder, which were:

# {{nihongo|'''Ohoikazuchi'''|大雷}}, from the head of Izanami;
# {{nihongo|'''Honoikazuchi'''|火雷}}, from her chest;
# {{nihongo|'''Kuroikazuchi'''|黒雷}}, from her abdomen;
# {{nihongo|'''Sakuikazuchi'''|折雷}}, from her genitals;
# {{nihongo|'''Wakaikazuchi'''|若雷}}, from her left arm;
# {{nihongo|'''Tsuchiikazuchi'''|土雷}}, from her right arm;
# {{nihongo|'''Naruikazuchi'''|鳴雷}}, from her left foot;
# {{nihongo|'''Fusuikazuchi'''|伏雷}}, from her right foot.

Izanagi, shocked, decided to return home, but Izanami was embarrassed by his appearance and commands the {{nihongo|Yomotsushikome|黄泉 丑女|lit. "horrible women from the world of darkness"}} to chase Izanagi. In his flight, he took the head-dress from his head, throws it to the ground where it turns into a bunch of grapes. The Yomotsushikome start to eat them but keep chasing the fleeing Izanagi. So he broke the tine the comb that he wore in his right bun and as he threw it to the ground it becomes bamboo shoots prompting the Yomotsushikome to eat them and enabling Izanagi to flee.

However, Izanami decides to release the eight gods of thunder and 1,500 warriors from Yomi to continue the pursuit. Izanagi draws and brandishes his ten-grasp<ref group="nb" name="grasp"/> sword to continue his flight. As they kept on pursuing him, Izanagi on reaching the {{nihongo|Yomotsu-hirasaka|黄泉比良坂}}, the slope that descends from the land of the living to Yomi, took three peaches from a tree that had grown in that place and throws them at his followers so that they flee.

Izanagi comments:

{{quote|Assistance to all people when they are tired and face difficulties|<ref group="nb">「人々が困っている時に助けてくれ」. ''[[Kojiki]]''</ref>}}

These peaches were called: {{nihongo|Ohokamuzumi-no-mikoto|意富加牟豆美命}}.

Finally Izanami persecutes Izanagi, but he lifts a rock that a thousand men could not move and blocks with it the slope. At that moment their eyes meet for the last time.

Izanami says:

{{quote|If you behave in this way, I will strangle and kill one thousand men of your land in one day!|<ref group="nb">「私はこれから毎日、一日に千人ずつ殺そう」. ''[[Kojiki]]''</ref>}}

Izanagi replies:

{{quote|If you do this, I will in one day set up 1,500 parturition houses. So in one day indeed 1,000 men will die and indeed 1,500 are going to be born.|<ref group="nb">「それなら私は人間が決して滅びないよう、一日に千五百人生ませよう」. ''[[Kojiki]]''</ref>}}

These words justify the circle of life and death in humans. For the same reason, Izanami is also called {{nihongo|'''Yomotsu-ohokami'''|黄泉津大神}} or {{nihongo|'''Chishiki-no-ohokami'''|道敷大神}} and the rock that covers the entrance to the world of the dead is known as {{nihongo|'''Chikaeshi-no-ohokami'''|道返之大神}} or {{nihongo|'''Yomido-no-ohokami'''|黄泉戸大神}} and is today known as {{nihongo|slope of Ifuya|伊賦夜坂}} in [[Izumo, Shimane|Izumo]], [[Shimane Prefecture]].

===Purification of Izanagi===
Leaving Yomi, Izanagi decided to remove all [[Kegare|uncleanness]] in his body through a purification ceremony (''[[misogi]]'') consisting in a bath in the river at Ahakihara in Tachibana no Ono in Tsukushi. As he stripped his clothes and accessories on the floor the following twelve gods are born:

# {{nihongo|'''[[Chimata-no-kami|Tsukitatsufunato]]'''|衝立船戸神}}, emerges from the [[Staff (stick)|staff]];
# {{nihongo|'''[[Michi-no-nagachiha]]'''|道之長乳歯神}}, from the [[Obi (sash)|obi]];
# {{nihongo|'''[[Tokihakashi]]'''|時量師神}}, from the handbag;
# {{nihongo|'''[[Wazurahinoushi]]'''|和豆良比能宇斯能神}}, from cloths;
# {{nihongo|'''[[Michimata]]'''|道俣神}}, from the [[hakama]];
# {{nihongo|'''[[Akiguhi-no-ushi]]'''|飽咋之宇斯能神}}, from the crown [[corona]];
# {{nihongo|'''[[Okizakaru]]'''|奥疎神}}, from the armband of the left hand;
# {{nihongo|'''[[Okitsunagisabiko]]'''|奥津那芸佐毘古神}}, from the armband of the left hand;;
# {{nihongo|'''[[Okitsukahibera]]'''|奥津甲斐弁羅神}}, from the armband of the left hand;
# {{nihongo|'''[[Hezakaru]]'''|辺疎神}}, from the armband of the right hand;
# {{nihongo|'''[[Hetsunagisabiko]]'''|辺津那芸佐毘古神}}, from the armband of the right hand;
# {{nihongo|'''[[Hetsukahibera]]'''|辺津甲斐弁羅神}}, from the armband of the right hand;

Subsequently Izanagi is stripped of impurities from the land of Yomi. In this moment two gods are born:

# {{nihongo|'''[[Yasomagatsuhi]]'''|八十禍津日神}}
# {{nihongo|'''[[Ohomagatsuhi]]'''|大禍津日神}}

Then, shaking off the curse, three gods are born:

# {{nihongo|'''[[Kamunaobi]]'''|神直毘神}}
# {{nihongo|'''[[Ohonaobi]]'''|大直毘神}}
# {{nihongo|'''[[Izunome]]'''|伊豆能売}}

Then, when washing with water the lower parts of his body, two gods are born;

# {{nihongo|'''[[Sokotsuwatatsumi]]'''|底津綿津見神}}
# {{nihongo|'''[[Sokotsutsunoo]]'''|底筒之男神}}

When washing the middle of his body, two more gods are born:

# {{nihongo|'''[[Nakatsuwatatsumi]]'''|中津綿津見神}}
# {{nihongo|'''[[Nakatsutsunoo]]'''|中筒之男神}}

Finally, washing the upper part of his body, two more gods are born:

# {{nihongo|'''[[Uhatsuwatatsumi]]'''|上津綿津見神}}
# {{nihongo|'''[[Uhatsutsunoo]]'''|上筒之男神}}

The trio of Sokotsuwatatsumi, Nakatsuwatatsumi and Uhatsuwatatsumi make up the group of deities called [[Sanjin Watatsumi]], or the gods of water. The trio of Sokotsutsunoo, Nakatsutsunoo and Uhatsutsunoo make up the [[Sumiyoshi Sanjin]] group of deities, gods of fishing and sea, to whom tribute is payed at [[Sumiyoshi Taisha]].

